
# Self-Healing Infrastructure

## Project Overview
This project demonstrates a self-healing infrastructure system using Docker, Prometheus, Alertmanager, Webhooks, and Ansible.

It monitors an NGINX service, detects failures, sends alerts, and uses an Ansible playbook to restart the NGINX container.

## Tools and Technologies
- Docker and Docker Compose
- NGINX
- Prometheus
- Prometheus NGINX Exporter
- Alertmanager
- Python Flask Webhook
- Ansible

## Project Architecture

1. NGINX runs as a Docker container.
2. NGINX Exporter collects NGINX metrics.
3. Prometheus collects and evaluates metrics.
4. Alertmanager receives alerts from Prometheus.
5. A Python Flask webhook receives alert notifications.
6. Ansible runs a playbook to restart the NGINX container.



- Integrated Alertmanager with a Python webhook.
- Used Ansible to automate container recovery.
